>
  <p>A louvred pergola lets you adjust overhead shade while keeping the furniture in place. Before ordering, check the space between posts, how the structure is fixed, where rainwater drains and who is responsible for installation.</p>
  <p>This guide helps you compare the options and prepare a useful supplier brief. It is research-based: AHC has not installed or tested these systems.</p>

  <section class="pergola-quick-summary" aria-labelledby="pergola-quick-summary-heading">
    <h2 id="pergola-quick-summary-heading">The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Choose the roof:</strong> Manual louvres are simpler; motorised models add convenience and electrical considerations. Rotating louvres do not necessarily retract.</li>
      <li><strong>Measure usable space:</strong> Allow for posts, base plates, open-blade height, doors and furniture in use.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the site:</strong> Confirm engineering, foundations, wind exposure, drainage and approvals before committing.</li>
      <li><strong>Compare total cost:</strong> Include delivery, installation, warranties and future servicing—not just the kit price.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <nav class="pergola-guide-contents" aria-label="On this page">
    <strong>Find the information you need</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#measure-the-space">Measurements</a></li>
      <li><a href="#engineering-and-wind">Engineering and wind claims</a></li>
      <li><a href="#pergolux-series-4">Pergolux Series 4 comparison</a></li>
      <li><a href="#pergolux-warranty">Pergolux warranty</a></li>
      <li><a href="#supplier-checklist">Supplier checklist</a></li>
    </ul>
